nreverted, security-relevant residue on all three nodes with no clear ongoing purpose.","evidence_ids":["cmd-28e7721c15854254","cmd-8beb0998b8994850","cmd-8b89fc66dead4fb2","cmd-4a5430a23dfb4470","cmd-4220c4f3f73346df","cmd-6dec2c422c8b49dc","cmd-28960fe679f54341","cmd-cf652d15ef664e84"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied: node1 is configured as a writable streaming-replication primary, node2 and node3 were cloned via pg_basebackup as read-only standbys with standby.signal/primary_conninfo, and writes on the primary were repeatedly and directly confirmed visible on both standbys, both before and after a full sequential node-restart cycle. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed to a high standard for all three nodes, with boot-identity changes cross-checked against the fixed lifecycle snapshots. Operational hygiene is moderate: a destructive but self-corrected re-initialization detour wasted a basebackup cycle on node2/node3, and an SSH keypair/authorized_keys entry added for a failed password-transfer attempt appears to have been left in place on all three nodes without cleanup.","limitations":["The pg_hba.conf/postgresql.conf content and replicator credentials are partially redacted in captured stdout, limiting direct verification of exact authentication parameters beyond scram-sha-256 usage.","No command in the captured timeline explicitly removes the SSH keys added in cmd-8b89fc66dead4fb2/cmd-4a5430a23dfb4470/cmd-4220c4f3f73346df; residue cannot be independently confirmed via the lifecycle snapshots since those only scan /tmp, not ~/.ssh.","Restart/persistence-across-reboot was not itself a stated requirement of the public task contract, so restart evidence quality informs confidence but does not gate the core replication requirements."]},"ttft_ms":57409,"type":"result","duration_ms":110864,"uuid":"306661eb-1854-4277-b5f0-bf17d41a09e5","ttft_stream_ms":1521,"time_to_request_ms":50,"first_content